      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "toggle means to turn on if its off or turn on if its off \nturn on means on \nturn off means turn off all \n\nhow to approach it\n1000x1000 grid \nwe can simply make an 2 dimensional array but dherai huncha \nfirst make a variable with turn on turn off \nturn off should be = 1,000,000\nturn on = 0\nand read the instruction one by one \n\nyo bekkar ho \n\nnext \n\nmake one hashMap turn on\nwe store (x,y) coordinate in key and in value turn on\nand itterate over the each instruction and if it says turn on store that coordinate if turn off remove that coordianate and if\ntoggle then go to each coordinate and check if the coordinate is present in turn on if so remove it and if its not present in \nhashmap then add it to the hashmap\n\nHow to itteerate over the array like this \n(a,b) to (n,m)\n\ncan i do like this \n\nfor i in a..n+1 {\n    for j in b..m+1 {\n        //todo()\n    }\n}\n\nwe have to get to n so ending should be n+1 and m+1\n\n\n\n",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "toggle means to turn on if its off or turn on if its off \nturn on means on \nturn off means turn off all \n\nhow to approach it\n1000x1000 grid \nwe can simply make an 2 dimensional array but dherai huncha \nfirst make a variable with turn on turn off \nturn off should be = 1,000,000\nturn on = 0\nand read the instruction one by one \n\nyo bekkar ho \n\nnext \n\nmake one hashMap turn on\nwe store (x,y) coordinate in key and in value turn on\nand itterate over the each instruction and if it says turn on store that coordinate if turn off remove that coordianate and if\ntoggle then go to each coordinate and check if the coordinate is present in turn on if so remove it and if its not present in \nhashmap then add it to the hashmap\n\nHow to itteerate over the array like this \n(a,b) to (n,m)\n\ncan i do like this \n\nfor i in a..n+1 {\n    for j in b..m+1 {\n        //todo()\n    }\n}\n\nwe have to get to n so ending should be n+1 and m+1\n\n\n\n",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    }
